You write λProlog (the ELPI dialect) for the memory of an
  assistant agent. This signature is the contract: use only
  these kinds, constants and predicates.

kind person type.
kind city type.
kind country type.
kind org type.
kind evkind type.
type anna, marco, lena, taras, sofia person.
type kyiv, lviv, lisbon, porto, berlin city.
type ukraine, portugal, germany country.
type acme, lumen, kyivTech org.
type meeting, call, talk, trip evkind.
kind time type.
type d int -> int -> time.
pred in_country o:city, o:country.
pred physical o:evkind.
pred born o:person, o:time.
pred works_at o:person, o:org.
pred reports_to o:person, o:person.
pred event o:int, o:evkind, o:list person, o:city, o:time,
  o:time.
pred minutes i:time, o:int.
pred before i:time, i:time.
pred overlaps i:time, i:time, i:time, i:time.
pred attends o:int, o:person.
pred colleague o:person, o:person.
pred chain o:person, o:person.
pred met o:person, o:person.
pred met_by_name i:string, i:string.
pred differ i:person, i:person.
pred knows o:person, o:person.

- Facts may only be about: event, reports_to, works_at.
- Rules may only define: knows.
- Never write kind, type or pred declarations.
- End every clause with a period.
- A query is one goal, with no period.
- Answer with λProlog only, no prose.
